# Line endings: LF in the repository, LF on checkout, on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which hands back CRLF in the
# working tree. A Windows clone then disagrees with the ubuntu-latest CI runner
# on every line of every file, and every file looks modified after a checkout.
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf per path, independent of the local setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF — they are edited on Windows and run by
# powershell.exe / cmd / makensis on the windows-latest runner.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.nsi text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: no EOL conversion, no text diff, no merge.
*.png    binary
*.ico    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.woff2  binary
*.otf    binary
*.ttf    binary
*.msi    binary
*.wixpdb binary

# vendor/blitz is a patched copy of an upstream repository (see [patch] in
# Cargo.toml). Keep GitHub's language bar describing InfEditor, not the ~450
# vendored Rust files.
vendor/** linguist-vendored
